# codechat.nvim Development Rules

## Architecture
Terminal driver that launches and injects context into CLI coding agents (Claude, Cursor, ttadk wrappers) running inside Snacks terminals.

## Key Subsystems
- `lua/codechat/terminal.lua` — Terminal lifecycle management, bracketed paste input injection
- `lua/codechat/ui.lua` — Comment popup (Snacks float) shown before sending context
- `lua/codechat/config.lua` — Agent registry with command, setup steps, login shell, fallbacks

## Constraints
- Depends on folke/snacks.nvim for terminal and floating window APIs
- Supports multiple agent backends with configurable launch commands
- Input injection uses bracketed paste sequences for reliable multi-line input
- Login shell mode (`$SHELL -lic`) required when setup uses shell functions (nvm, conda)
- Agent picker persists choice across Neovim restarts
- Terminal pre-warming: agent can launch while user types their comment
